["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A clean kill, a found bird, a cool carcass and a legal bag. This chapter ties the whole Masterclass together and ends with a one page cheat sheet.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The shot window. You stand in brush. A wedge of open sky above and ahead of you is the safe window. A high bird with sky behind it: OK. A low bird over the brush: no shot. Range about 15 to 30 metres, a Tip. Loads from Washington Fish and Wildlife, 75 percent: lead 7.5 or 8, steel 6 or 7, skeet or improved cylinder choke. Straightaway birds: most hunters shoot high, so hold a hair under.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The shot window</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"170\" fill=\"#dbe8f4\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"170\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 228)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<path d=\"M200 220 L80 60 L320 60 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n<path d=\"M200 220 L80 60 M200 220 L320 60\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 90)\"><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"76\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">high bird, sky behind: OK</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(330 180)\"><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/></g>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"164\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">low bird: NO</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15 to 30 m</text>\n<text x=\"70\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Lead 7.5 or 8 (steel 6 or 7), open choke</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Straightaway: hold a hair under (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Shoot high birds with sky behind, about 15 to 30 m (Tip).</li><li>Lead 7.5 or 8, steel 6 or 7; skeet or improved cylinder choke <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: shot placement and range in full</summary><ul><li>Aim for the head and front half: brain, neck, heart and lungs (Tip, anatomy from chapter 2, 70%).</li><li>\"One small pellet is often enough to bring down a quail.\" (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife)</li><li>Loads: \"Size 7 1/2 and 8 lead shot are standard among quail hunters, and some go as small as 9's. If you're shooting steel, 6's and 7's are the norm.\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li>Chokes: \"A fairly open choke, skeet or improved cylinder, is well suited to most quail shooting situations.\" <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span> Your 12 gauge works and puts more pellets in the pattern <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The quick lesson's loads (Tip): quail and partridge, lead 7.5 or 6, or steel 6; chukar and pheasant, lead 5 or 6, or steel 3 or 4. Huns: lead 6 or 7.5 at 30 to 45 yards (75%, Washington).</li><li>Range: 15 to 30 m is a Tip, not a rule. Pattern your gun at 20 and 30 m first: <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-skills\">Shotgun skills</a> and the pattern math diagram there.</li><li>Lead shot is legal for upland birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Plug: no more than 3 shells in total <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation. A quail is hit and falls into brush. You keep your eyes on the spot where it fell, drop your orange hat where you stood, and walk straight to the spot before shooting at any other bird. Missouri Conservation Department tip, 60 percent. Retrieval is the law: all reasonable effort to find it, 99 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mark the fall</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"200\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"80\" ry=\"30\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(80 210)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<circle r=\"7\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"><animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"150;260;300;300\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.45;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"70;60;196;196\" keyTimes=\"0;.3;.45;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></circle>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.5s\"/><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"210\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"196\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">X</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6s\"/><rect x=\"66\" y=\"222\" width=\"28\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"7s\"/><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\"></text></g><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"80 210;290 198\" begin=\"7s\" dur=\"2.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g></g>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"250\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird falls. Eyes stay on the spot.</text>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"250\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Drop your hat where you stood</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"8s\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"250\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Walk straight to it. No second bird first.</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Eyes on the spot. Drop your hat. Walk straight to it. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Mark the fall before you look for a second bird <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Retrieval is the law <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: after the shot in full</summary><ul><li>Mentally mark where the bird falls before swinging on another, and drop a hat or handkerchief where you stood (60%, Missouri Conservationist).</li><li>Walk straight to the spot with your eyes on it (Tip, from the quick lesson).</li><li>A hit bird may run. Get to it fast; a wing tipped quail can hide in brush (Tip).</li><li>Dispatch a live bird at once, quickly and humanely (Tip).</li><li>No dog: shoot only over short cover so every bird falls where you can find it (Tip).</li><li>Search in a widening circle from the last feather patch (Tip).</li></ul><aside class=\"callout law\"><div class=\"callout-t\">The rule</div><p>\"No person shall kill, cripple or wound game without making all reasonable effort to locate, dispatch, retrieve and include it in their bag limit.\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></p></aside></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Care for a quail in 4 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bird care step 1: cool it fast. Put the bird in a game vest with a mesh back, not a plastic bag, and keep it out of the October sun. Tip.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird care: 1 Cool it fast</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<path d=\"M140 70 h120 l20 140 h-160 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<g stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"162\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"162\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"174\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"174\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"186\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"186\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"198\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"198\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"222\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"222\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"234\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"234\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"246\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"246\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"258\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"258\" y2=\"200\"/></g>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">mesh back vest</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">no plastic</text>\n<text x=\"330\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bag</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mesh vest, shade, air around it (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Cool it fast: mesh vest, shade, air around it.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bird care step 2: draw the bird soon, an optional Tip. Open below the breastbone and hook the guts out with a finger. Keep the breasts and legs.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird care: 2 Draw it (Tip)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 150) scale(2.2 2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<line x1=\"140\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"170\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"190,170 184.5,178.4 180.0,170.9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">small cut</text>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"232\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">below breastbone</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Finger out the guts, keep the meat (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Draw it soon if warm: finger out the guts (Tip).</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bird care step 3: leave one feathered wing attached to each bird until it is home, the Rule Book, page 15, 99 percent. Bring home both breasts, the edible portions.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird care: 3 One wing stays on</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 150) scale(2.2 2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-1 -6 5 -6 q-3 1 -3 6 Z\" fill=\"#4a4a4a\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<ellipse cx=\"190\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One feathered wing (99%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Both breasts go home (99%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Law: wing on until home (Rule Book)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> One feathered wing stays on until home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bird care step 4: in the cooler on ice for the drive home, then cook to 74 degrees Celsius, 165 Fahrenheit, inside, USDA poultry guidance, 90 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird care: 4 Ice, then cook to 74 °C</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"80\" width=\"180\" height=\"120\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<rect x=\"110\" y=\"80\" width=\"180\" height=\"26\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f5f8a\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">cooler + ice</text>\n<rect x=\"300\" y=\"90\" width=\"30\" height=\"100\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"309\" y=\"120\" width=\"12\" height=\"62\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"315\" y=\"212\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">74 °C</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cook to 74 °C inside (90%)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Ice in the cooler, then cook to 74 °C.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Cool birds fast in October sun (Tip).</li><li>One feathered wing stays on each bird until it is home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: field care in full</summary><ul><li>\"One feathered wing stays on each bird until it is home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. Both breasts must come home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.\" From the quick lesson and the <a href=\"#/s/rb-after-the-kill\">Rule Book: after the kill</a>.</li><li>Page 15: \"Anyone who possesses or transports a game bird, other than a migratory game bird, must leave attached to the carcass one feathered wing\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Breasting birds in the field: keep the wing attached to the breast you carry (85%, my reading in the Rule Book).</li><li>A game vest with a mesh back beats a plastic bag (Tip).</li><li>Count birds by species as you clean them and write the tally in the Journal with the MU (Management Unit) (Tip).</li><li>Cooler with ice for the drive home (Tip, from the trip checklist).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 330\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart of meat per bird in grams, hunter estimates, Tip, about 60 percent. Quail 60 to 80. Chukar and partridge 150 to 250. Ruffed grouse 200 to 280. Mallard 350 to 450. Pheasant cock 450 to 600. Canada goose about 1 kilogram of boned breast. A dusky grouse gives about twice a ruffed grouse; a teal is one serving.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"330\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Meat per bird, grams (Tip, 60%)</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Quail</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"50\" width=\"13\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"163\" y=\"50\" width=\"4\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"172.8\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">60 to 80</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"104\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Chukar, partridge</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"90\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"182\" y=\"90\" width=\"21\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"208.5\" y=\"106\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">150 to 250</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"144\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Ruffed grouse</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"130\" width=\"42\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"192\" y=\"130\" width=\"17\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"214.8\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">200 to 280</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Mallard</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"170\" width=\"74\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"224\" y=\"170\" width=\"21\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"250.5\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">350 to 450</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"224\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Pheasant cock</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"210\" width=\"94\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"244\" y=\"210\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"282.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">450 to 600</text>\n  <text x=\"142\" y=\"264\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Canada goose</text>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"250\" width=\"189\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"339\" y=\"250\" width=\"42\" height=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".45\"/>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">about 1 kg breast</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusky grouse: about twice a ruffed grouse</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"316\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Teal: one serving</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A quail gives about 60 to 80 g of meat (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Cook birds to 74 °C (165 °F) inside <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: meat and cooking in full</summary><ul><li>Quail: pluck or skin, gut with a thumb. About 60 to 80 g of meat, one per person as a starter (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Chukar and partridge: skin and breast, keep the legs. About 150 to 250 g of meat per bird (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Food safety: USDA lists all poultry at 165 °F (74 °C) (85%, search preview of the USDA table). The app's meat care lesson: cook birds to 74 °C <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Breast meat is lean and dries fast. Cook it quick and hot, or braise whole birds slowly (Tip).</li><li>Plucked, skin on, the meat stays moister (Tip).</li><li>Lessons: <a href=\"#/s/meat-care\">Meat care</a> and <a href=\"#/s/cooking\">Cooking wild game</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 395\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Cards: Quail trip: gun and field rules. Shotgun, air gun or bow: Quail, chukar, partridge, pheasant (95%, my reading). Lead shot: OK for upland birds. Ducks need non toxic shot. Plug: Pump or semi auto: no more than 2 shells in the magazine. Hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset. Evidence: One feathered wing on each bird until home. 100 m: From homes, occupied farm buildings, schools, playgrounds.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"395\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail trip: gun and field rules</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"47\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pages 10 to 15</text>\n<rect x=\"6.0\" y=\"69\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"112\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M6.0 115 V78 Q6.0 69 15.0 69 H187.0 Q196.0 69 196.0 78 V115 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Shotgun, air gun or</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"107\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">bow</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Quail, chukar,</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">partridge, pheasant</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">(95%, my reading)</text>\n<rect x=\"204.0\" y=\"69\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"112\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M204.0 115 V78 Q204.0 69 213.0 69 H385.0 Q394.0 69 394.0 78 V115 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"89\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Lead shot</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"135\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">OK for upland birds.</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"153\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Ducks need non toxic</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">shot</text>\n<rect x=\"6.0\" y=\"189\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"94\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M6.0 217 V198 Q6.0 189 15.0 189 H187.0 Q196.0 189 196.0 198 V217 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Plug</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Pump or semi auto: no</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">more than 2 shells in</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"273\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">the magazine</text>\n<rect x=\"204.0\" y=\"189\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"94\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M204.0 217 V198 Q204.0 189 213.0 189 H385.0 Q394.0 189 394.0 198 V217 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"209\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Hours</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"237\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">1 hour before sunrise</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"255\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">to 1 hour after sunset</text>\n<rect x=\"6.0\" y=\"291\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"94\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M6.0 319 V300 Q6.0 291 15.0 291 H187.0 Q196.0 291 196.0 300 V319 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"311\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Evidence</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"339\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">One feathered wing on</text>\n<text x=\"14.0\" y=\"357\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">each bird until home</text>\n<rect x=\"204.0\" y=\"291\" width=\"190.0\" height=\"94\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#c92a2a\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/>\n<path d=\"M204.0 319 V300 Q204.0 291 213.0 291 H385.0 Q394.0 291 394.0 300 V319 Z\" fill=\"#c92a2a\"/>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"311\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">100 m</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"339\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">From homes, occupied</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"357\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">farm buildings,</text>\n<text x=\"212.0\" y=\"375\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">schools, playgrounds</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>Region 8 quail: 1 October to 30 November, 10 a day, 30 in possession <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>BC hunting licence only; shotgun, air gun or bow; no rifle (95 to 99%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every rule, from the Rule Book</summary><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>What the app's Rule Book says</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Region 8 quail</td><td>\"QUAIL\", MUs 8-1 to 8-15, 8-21 to 8-26, Oct 1 to Nov 30, 10 (30) <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Region 8 chukar</td><td>5 (15), same MUs and dates <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Region 8 gray partridge</td><td>3 (9), same MUs and dates <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Region 8 pheasant</td><td>Cocks only, 2 (6), same MUs and dates <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Region 3 (Heffley Creek)</td><td>Chukar, partridge, pheasant cocks; no quail row <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">97%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Region 2 (Mission)</td><td>Pheasant cocks only, MUs 2-4, 2-8; no quail row <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">97%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Licence</td><td>BC hunting licence, no species licence <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Methods</td><td>Shotgun, air gun, bows B, C, D; no rimfire or centrefire <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Shot</td><td>Lead legal for upland birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Plug</td><td>3 shells in total <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Hours</td><td>1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Wing</td><td>One feathered wing on until home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Edible portions</td><td>Both breasts go home <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>100 m</td><td>No hunting or shooting near occupied buildings <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Cultivated land</td><td>Consent of owner, lessee or occupant <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Calls</td><td>No recorded or electronic calls for game birds <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Dogs</td><td>Unleashed dogs fine for quail <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Possession for upland birds while hunting or returning is three times the daily limit, except pheasants in Region 4 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Each hunter has a personal bag limit <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. You cannot fill your partner's limit <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">90%</span>.</li><li>Read the screens themselves: <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Region 8</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Legal methods</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-bag-limits\">Bag limits</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-after-the-kill\">After the kill</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-where-you-can-hunt\">Where you can hunt</a>, <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">Unlawful acts</a>.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fact</th><th>Sure</th><th>Ch</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Weight 140 to 230 g, length 24 to 27 cm</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Male: black face, white rim, curled black plume</td><td>80%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Female: plain face, small plume</td><td>80%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Straight plume = mountain quail, no season</td><td>99%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Young: buff tips on primary coverts</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Hun 300 to 500 g, orange face</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Chukar 538 to 765 g, black necklace, red legs</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>In BC since 1860 to 1912</td><td>85%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Fraser Valley birds apparently gone</td><td>85%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">1</a></td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Heart and lungs in the front half</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-02\">2</a></td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>No diaphragm, 9 air sacs</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-02\">2</a></td></tr><tr><td>12</td><td>Crop stores, gizzard grinds with grit</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-02\">2</a></td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>White breast muscle: short flights</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-02\">2</a></td></tr><tr><td>14</td><td>Few live past one year</td><td>65%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-02\">2</a></td></tr><tr><td>15</td><td>4 colour cones incl. UV (ultraviolet)</td><td>85%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-03\">3</a></td></tr><tr><td>16</td><td>Hear best at 1 to 4 kHz (kilohertz)</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-03\">3</a></td></tr><tr><td>17</td><td>Smell weak</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-03\">3</a></td></tr><tr><td>18</td><td>Feed 15 to 30 m from cover</td><td>80%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">4</a></td></tr><tr><td>19</td><td>Sentinel on a post</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">4</a></td></tr><tr><td>20</td><td>Run first, fly last</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">4</a></td></tr><tr><td>21</td><td>Assembly call \"chi CA go\"</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">4</a></td></tr><tr><td>22</td><td>Singles land a few dozen yards off, hold tight</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">4</a></td></tr><tr><td>23</td><td>Coveys usually under 30 in BC</td><td>85%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">4</a></td></tr><tr><td>24</td><td>Break up in March, about 14 eggs, 22 to 23 days</td><td>70 to 80%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-05\">5</a></td></tr><tr><td>25</td><td>Two feeds: after dawn, late afternoon</td><td>70%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-06\">6</a></td></tr><tr><td>26</td><td>Midday: dust, rest, water</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-06\">6</a></td></tr><tr><td>27</td><td>Hot weather: water daily</td><td>80%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-06\">6</a></td></tr><tr><td>28</td><td>250 to 500 m, rare above 750 m</td><td>85%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-07\">7</a></td></tr><tr><td>29</td><td>Winter range about 10.5 ha</td><td>80%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-07\">7</a></td></tr><tr><td>30</td><td>Stop 15 to 20 s on a stop and go</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-09\">9</a></td></tr><tr><td>31</td><td>Chukar: get above, follow the contour</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-09\">9</a></td></tr><tr><td>32</td><td>Lead 7.5 or 8, open choke</td><td>75%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-10\">10</a></td></tr><tr><td>33</td><td>Region 8: 1 Oct to 30 Nov, 10 (30)</td><td>99%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-10\">10</a></td></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>No quail row in Region 3 or 2</td><td>97%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-07\">7</a></td></tr><tr><td>35</td><td>Shotgun only, no .22</td><td>95%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-10\">10</a></td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>One feathered wing on until home</td><td>99%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-10\">10</a></td></tr><tr><td>37</td><td>100 m from occupied buildings</td><td>99%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-09\">9</a></td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>Orchard = cultivated land: ask</td><td>95%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-09\">9</a></td></tr><tr><td>39</td><td>Bylaws not in the synopsis: hunt outside towns</td><td>99%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-09\">9</a></td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>Cook to 74 °C</td><td>85%</td><td><a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-10\">10</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Tap the chapter number to go back to the full story.</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Year wheel for California quail in BC. January and February: big winter coveys. March: coveys break up. April: pairs. May: nests. June: peak hatch. July: broods. August: families join together. September: coveys form. October and November: the Region 8 season, 1 October to 30 November, 99 percent. December: winter coveys. Biology 65 to 80 percent.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The quail year</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 68.0 A96 96 0 0 1 248.0 80.9 L225.0 120.7 A50 50 0 0 0 200.0 114.0 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"218.89379029248403\" y=\"98.48741468089801\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jan</text>\n<text x=\"227.95245687107223\" y=\"62.748159108202486\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">coveys</text>\n<path d=\"M248.0 80.9 A96 96 0 0 1 283.1 116.0 L243.3 139.0 A50 50 0 0 0 225.0 120.7 Z\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"251.618795026618\" y=\"117.38120497338204\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feb</text>\n<tex