\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"181.106209707516\" y=\"98.48741468089801\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dec</text>\n<text x=\"172.04754312892777\" y=\"62.748159108202486\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">coveys</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Oct 1 to</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nov 30</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(99%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Open any chapter again, or plan the trip in the planner (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all the links</summary><ul><li>1: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-01\">Meet the bird</a>: ID, look alikes, size, BC history. Cheat lines 1 to 9.</li><li>2: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-02\">The body</a>: air sacs, crop, gizzard, heart, muscle. Lines 10 to 14.</li><li>3: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-03\">The senses</a>: eyes, ears, nose, sentinel. Lines 15 to 17.</li><li>4: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-04\">The mind</a>: calls, scatter and regroup, pressure. Lines 18 to 23.</li><li>5: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-05\">The year</a>: coveys, pairs, nests, season. Line 24.</li><li>6: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-06\">The day</a>: feeds, grit, dust, weather. Lines 25 to 27.</li><li>7: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-07\">Where they are</a>: habitat, plants, Hunt Map, your three areas. Lines 28, 29 and 34.</li><li>8: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-08\">Sign and tracking</a>: tracks, droppings, dust bowls, calls.</li><li>9: <a href=\"#/s/mc-quail-09\">How to hunt them</a>: permission, bylaws, stop and go, singles, chukar. Lines 30, 31, 37 to 39.</li><li>10: this chapter. Lines 32, 33, 35, 36 and 40.</li><li>Quick version: <a href=\"#/s/upland-birds\">Quail, chukar, partridge, pheasant</a>, <a href=\"#/s/first-quail-trip\">Your first quail trip</a>, <a href=\"#/s/local-okanagan\">Okanagan trip plan</a>, <a href=\"#/s/gallery-upland\">Photo ID gallery</a>, <a href=\"#/s/habitat-upland\">Habitat tour</a>.</li><li>Plan it: <a href=\"#/plan\">the hunt planner</a>. Map it: <a href=\"#/map\">the Hunt Map</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bird care step 3: leave one feathered wing attached to each bird until it is home, the Rule Book, page 15, 99 percent. Bring home both breasts, the edible portions.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bird care: 3 One wing stays on</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(200 150) scale(2.2 2.2)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-1 -6 5 -6 q-3 1 -3 6 Z\" fill=\"#4a4a4a\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<ellipse cx=\"190\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"34\" ry=\"16\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">One feathered wing (99%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Both breasts go home (99%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Law: wing on until home (Rule Book)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Mark it, walk it, cool it, keep a wing; cook to seventy four, then let the kitchen sing.\" (Tip, 85 to 99% for the facts)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"10, 30, 74\": 10 a day, 30 in possession <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>, cook to 74 °C <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Load hook:</strong> \"Seven and a half for the little ones.\" Lead 7.5 is standard for quail <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"A bird you cannot find is a bird you should not have shot.\" Hunting educators teach shooting only where you can recover the bird (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Washington Fish and Wildlife, Missouri Conservationist, USDA, the app Rule Book, quick lesson and meat care lessons. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68963\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington Fish and Wildlife: quail hunting</a> and <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68921\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge hunting</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: loads, chokes, shooting <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://mdc.mo.gov/node/245855\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Missouri Conservationist: Quail hunting without dogs (Smith 1996)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: marking the fall <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.fsis.usda.gov/es/node/3293\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">USDA Food Safety and Inspection Service: safe minimum internal temperatures</a>, search preview 2026-10-11: all poultry 165 °F <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>App lessons: <a href=\"#/s/meat-care\">Meat care</a> (74 °C for birds, 80%), <a href=\"#/s/shotgun-skills\">Shotgun skills</a>, <a href=\"#/s/upland-birds\">quick lesson</a> (yields, loads: Tip).</li><li>Rules: the app <a href=\"#/s/rb-region-8\">Rule Book</a> screens linked above, synopsis 2026 to 2028, 2 October 2026 edition, pages 8, 9, 10, 12, 13, 15 and 68 (95 to 99%).</li><li>Cheat sheet lines: sources as listed in chapters 1 to 9.</li></ul></details>"]